<Styles xmlns="https://github.com/avaloniaui"
        xmlns:x="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml"
        xmlns:controls="clr-namespace:DroidLens.Client.Views.Controls">

    <!--
        ============================= CUSTOM SCROLLBAR =============================
        ControlTheme keyed {x:Type ScrollBar} — overrides the resource FluentTheme's own
        default styles point ScrollBar.Theme at, so every ScrollBar in the app picks this
        up automatically (no Classes, no per-view changes needed).

        1) DRAG MUST SCROLL CONTENT. ScrollBar's drag pipeline is:
              Thumb.DragDelta -> Track.ApplyThumbDrag -> Track.Value
           and only a value written back into ScrollBar.Value propagates to the owning
           ScrollViewer's Offset. So the Track's Value binding MUST be TwoWay (exactly
           like Fluent's own template: Value="{TemplateBinding Value, Mode=TwoWay}").
           With the default one-way binding the thumb visually moves during a drag but
           ScrollBar/ScrollViewer never see the new value -> content stays put. The
           IsDirectionReversed="True" on the vertical Track IS also required (matches
           Fluent, and makes the vertical drag/thumb math non-inverted), both matter.

        2) NO HOVER "TWITCH". The old version animated the Thumb's own Width/Height on
           :pointerover/:pressed. Width/Height are layout + hit-testing drivers for the
           exact part Track arranges, so animating them fed back into Track layout and
           showed a wobble on every enter/leave. The hover grow is now a pure
           RenderTransform scale on the Thumb (bounds, layout and hit-testing never
           change), eased with a gentle spring.

        Design goals (per request):
          1. No track background, no LineUp/LineDown arrow buttons — just a floating thumb.
          2. Thumb is neutral gray at rest (and on hover); the accent color — indigo at idle,
             amber while a stream is live, via the "ScrollbarAccentBrush" resource (same
             indigo/amber pairing as the VCam switch and the metric-row icons) — shows ONLY
             while dragging. MainWindow swaps that resource whenever IsStreaming or the
             theme changes.
          3. "Inertia" + slight grow: a SpringEasing transition on the thumb's RenderTransform
             scale so it eases into hover/drag size with a touch of overshoot instead of snapping.
          4. Edge bounce: when scrolling reaches the very top/bottom (or left/right), the
             thumb nudges a few px past the edge and springs back — iOS-style rubber-band,
             see ScrollBarBounceBehavior.cs. Does NOT fire on an ordinary mid-list stop, only
             when Value actually lands on Minimum/Maximum. That class owns a single
             TransformGroup=[ScaleTransform, TranslateTransform] on the Thumb's RenderTransform,
             so hover/press scale (driven from XAML below via the ScaleX/ScaleY attached
             properties) and the edge-bounce translate (driven from C# only) never overwrite
             each other. Do NOT set Thumb.RenderTransform directly anywhere in this file —
             that would replace the whole group and silently break one of the two effects.
    -->

    <!-- ScrollBarBounceBehavior.IsEnabled/ScaleX/ScaleY are attached properties from
         ScrollBarBounceBehavior.cs (namespace DroidLens.Client.Views.Controls, aliased
         "controls" above) — not a Style, so nothing to declare in this Styles file beyond
         using them as Setters/attributes below. -->

    <Style>
        <Style.Resources>

            <!-- ============================= SCROLLBAR THUMB ============================= -->
            <!-- Thumb color: neutral gray at rest (and on plain hover) — the dynamic
                 indigo/amber accent appears ONLY while actually dragging. The accent
                 follows the stream state exactly like the VCam switch's on-state:
                 indigo at idle, amber while a stream is live. The brush comes from the
                 shared "ScrollbarAccentBrush" resource (App.axaml), which MainWindow
                 swaps at runtime whenever IsStreaming or the theme changes. -->
            <ControlTheme x:Key="CustomScrollBarThumbTheme" TargetType="Thumb">
                <Setter Property="Background"        Value="#4A4863"/>
                <Setter Property="CornerRadius"      Value="3"/>
                <!-- Template fills the Thumb's own Bounds completely (no Margin here) —
                     Track computes drag hit-testing and position from the Thumb's actual
                     Bounds, so shrinking/offsetting via Margin ON THE THUMB ITSELF corrupts
                     that math. The 2px visual inset lives one level down, on the inner
                     Border, which is purely cosmetic and doesn't feed back into Track. -->
                <Setter Property="Template">
                    <ControlTemplate>
                        <Border Name="ThumbBorder"
                                Background="{TemplateBinding Background}"
                                CornerRadius="{TemplateBinding CornerRadius}"
                                Margin="2">
                            <Border.Transitions>
                                <Transitions>
                                    <BrushTransition Property="Background" Duration="0:0:0.2" Easing="CubicEaseOut"/>
                                </Transitions>
                            </Border.Transitions>
                        </Border>
                    </ControlTemplate>
                </Setter>

                <Style Selector="^:pointerover /template/ Border#ThumbBorder">
                    <Setter Property="Background" Value="#4A4863"/>
                </Style>
                <Style Selector="^:pressed /template/ Border#ThumbBorder">
                    <Setter Property="Background" Value="{DynamicResource ScrollbarAccentBrush}"/>
                </Style>
            </ControlTheme>

            <!-- ============================= SCROLLBAR ============================= -->
            <ControlTheme x:Key="{x:Type ScrollBar}" TargetType="ScrollBar">
                <Setter Property="Background"    Value="Transparent"/>
                <Setter Property="MinWidth"      Value="14"/>
                <Setter Property="MinHeight"     Value="14"/>

                <!-- ── VERTICAL ── -->
                <Style Selector="^:vertical">
                    <Setter Property="Template">
                        <ControlTemplate>
                            <Grid Background="{TemplateBinding Background}">
                                <Track Name="PART_Track"
                                       Minimum="{TemplateBinding Minimum}"
                                       Maximum="{TemplateBinding Maximum}"
                                       Value="{TemplateBinding Value, Mode=TwoWay}"
                                       ViewportSize="{TemplateBinding ViewportSize}"
                                       Orientation="Vertical"
                                       IsDirectionReversed="True">
                                    <Track.Thumb>
                                        <Thumb Name="PART_ThumbVisual"
                                               Theme="{StaticResource CustomScrollBarThumbTheme}"
                                               Width="10"
                                               HorizontalAlignment="Right"
                                               controls:ScrollBarBounceBehavior.IsEnabled="True"/>
                                    </Track.Thumb>
                                </Track>
                            </Grid>
                        </ControlTemplate>
                    </Setter>
                </Style>
                <Style Selector="^:vertical /template/ Thumb#PART_ThumbVisual:pointerover">
                    <Setter Property="controls:ScrollBarBounceBehavior.ScaleX" Value="1.25"/>
                </Style>
                <Style Selector="^:vertical /template/ Thumb#PART_ThumbVisual:pressed">
                    <Setter Property="controls:ScrollBarBounceBehavior.ScaleX" Value="1.5"/>
                </Style>

                <!-- ── HORIZONTAL ── -->
                <Style Selector="^:horizontal">
                    <Setter Property="Template">
                        <ControlTemplate>
                            <Grid Background="{TemplateBinding Background}">
                                <Track Name="PART_Track"
                                       Minimum="{TemplateBinding Minimum}"
                                       Maximum="{TemplateBinding Maximum}"
                                       Value="{TemplateBinding Value, Mode=TwoWay}"
                                       ViewportSize="{TemplateBinding ViewportSize}"
                                       Orientation="Horizontal">
                                    <Track.Thumb>
                                        <Thumb Name="PART_ThumbVisual"
                                               Theme="{StaticResource CustomScrollBarThumbTheme}"
                                               Height="10"
                                               VerticalAlignment="Bottom"
                                               controls:ScrollBarBounceBehavior.IsEnabled="True"/>
                                    </Track.Thumb>
                                </Track>
                            </Grid>
                        </ControlTemplate>
                    </Setter>
                </Style>
                <Style Selector="^:horizontal /template/ Thumb#PART_ThumbVisual:pointerover">
                    <Setter Property="controls:ScrollBarBounceBehavior.ScaleY" Value="1.25"/>
                </Style>
                <Style Selector="^:horizontal /template/ Thumb#PART_ThumbVisual:pressed">
                    <Setter Property="controls:ScrollBarBounceBehavior.ScaleY" Value="1.5"/>
                </Style>
            </ControlTheme>

        </Style.Resources>
    </Style>

    <!-- No visible seam/box where vertical and horizontal scrollbars meet in a ScrollViewer
         corner — keep it transparent so only the floating thumbs are ever visible. -->
    <Style Selector="ScrollViewer /template/ Rectangle#ScrollBarsSeparator">
        <Setter Property="Fill" Value="Transparent"/>
    </Style>

</Styles>
